<second_data>
Sure, I'd be happy to help you with that! Here's a step-by-step guide to integrate Stripe's hosted checkout with Laravel, supporting both credit cards and the iDEAL payment method:

1. Install the Stripe PHP library:

First, you need to install the Stripe PHP library using Composer. Run the following command in your terminal:

```bash
composer require stripe/stripe-php
```

2. Set up your Stripe API keys:

In your `.env` file, add your Stripe API keys:

```
STRIPE_KEY=your_stripe_api_key
STRIPE_SECRET=your_stripe_secret_key
```

3. Create a new route and controller:

Create a new route in your `routes/web.php` file:

```php
Route::get('/checkout', 'StripeController@checkout')->name('checkout');
Route::post('/checkout', 'StripeController@processPayment')->name('process_payment');
```

Create a new controller called `StripeController`:

```bash
php artisan make:controller StripeController
```

4. Implement the checkout method:

In your `StripeController`, add the following method to create a Stripe checkout session:

```php
public function checkout(Request $request)
{
    Stripe::setApiKey(config('services.stripe.secret'));

    $session = Session::create([
        'payment_method_types' => ['card', 'ideal'],
        'line_items' => [
            [
                'name' => 'Your Product Name',
                'amount' => 1000, // in cents
                'currency' => 'eur',
                'quantity' => 1,
            ],
        ],
        'success_url' => route('payment_success'),
        'cancel_url' => route('payment_cancel'),
    ]);

    return view('checkout', ['sessionId' => $session->id]);
}
```

5. Implement the processPayment method:

In your `StripeController`, add the following method to handle the payment:

```php
public function processPayment(Request $request)
{
    Stripe::setApiKey(config('services.stripe.secret'));

    $session = Session::retrieve($request->session_id);

    if ($session->payment_status === 'paid') {
        // Handle successful payment
        return redirect()->route('payment_success');
    }

    // Handle failed payment
    return redirect()->route('payment_cancel');
}
```

6. Create the checkout view:

Create a new view called `checkout.blade.php` and add the following code to render the Stripe checkout form:

```html
<form action="{{ route('process_payment') }}" method="post">
    @csrf
    <script
        src="https://checkout.stripe.com/checkout.js" class="stripe-button"
        data-key="{{ config('services.stripe.key') }}"
        data-amount="1000"
        data-name="Your Product Name"
        data-description="Your Product Description"
        data-image="https://example.com/your-image.png"
        data-locale="auto"
        data-currency="eur"
        data-allow-remember-me="false"
        data-panel-label="Pay {{ number_format(10, 2) }} €"
        data-label="Pay Now"
        data-zip-code="true"
        data-billing-address="true"
        data-shipping-address="true"
        data-bitcoin="true"
        data-alipay="true"
        data-ideal="true"
        data-session-id="{{ $sessionId }}"
    >
    </script>
</form>
```

7. Create success and cancel routes and views:

Create new routes and views for successful and cancelled payments. For example:

```php
Route::get('/payment/success', 'StripeController@paymentSuccess')->name('payment_success');
Route::get('/payment/cancel', 'StripeController@paymentCancel')->name('payment_cancel');
```

And in your `StripeController`:

```php
public function paymentSuccess()
{
    return view('payment_success');
}

public function paymentCancel()
{
    return view('payment_cancel');
}
```

Now you have a working Stripe integration with Laravel, supporting both credit cards and the iDEAL payment method.
