```

6. **Handle Webhook (Optional but recommended):**

To handle refunds, chargebacks, or other events, you should set up a webhook. You can find more information about webhooks in the [Stripe documentation](https://stripe.com/docs/webhooks).

That's it! Now you should have a working Stripe integration with Laravel that supports credit card and iDEAL payments using Stripe's Hosted Checkout. When a user clicks the payment button, they will be redirected to the Stripe checkout page, where they can choose their preferred payment method. After a successful payment, they will be redirected to the success page, and in case of cancellation, they will be redirected to the cancel page.
