According to Byrd and Turner (2001), it is essential for organizations to identify the unique IT capabilities that differentiate them from their competitors in order to achieve and sustain a competitive advantage. By leveraging these unique IT capabilities, organizations can improve internal operations, automate processes, and enhance products and services in a way that creates a unique value proposition for customers. This can help the firm to distinguish itself from competitors and attract and retain customers.

